  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A flipped WCS Z does not post. That does not change.\n- The refusal now names the exact reason. The issue permits this result: \"or the refusal names the exact reason and the decision is recorded\".\n- The post engine (`post::wcs_flip::apply`) and the verification gate (`app::setup_wcs_flip::setup_problem`) read the reason from one constant, `post::wcs_flip::Z_REASON`.\n- The post engine adds a second clause only for a section that has a canned cycle.\n- `docs/decisions/2474-wcs-flip-z-refusal.md` records the decision and answers the two open questions of the issue.\n\nThe new text of the post engine:\n\n`operation Probe: the WCS has its Z axis flipped; posting a flipped Z is not supported yet - on a control that reads Z reversed, the tool-length word depends on how the tool lengths were measured (a preset length needs G44, a length touched off on that control needs G43), the project does not state which, and the wrong word moves the tool by twice its length; the section also has a canned cycle, whose R plane a mirrored Z puts on the far side of the hole bottom - clear Flip Z on the WCS page`\n\n## Cause\n\n- The old text gave a general reason: \"tool-length compensation (G43) and the canned cycles' retract assume the controller's +Z leaves the work\".\n- The exact reason is this. The tool is on the physical \"up\" side of its tip. On a control that reads Z reversed, \"up\" is the control's -Z.\n- A register with a preset length then needs G44. A register with a length touched off on that control needs G43.\n- The project states only \"Z is flipped\". It does not state how the tool lengths were measured.\n- The wrong word moves the tool by twice its length. The post cannot select the word, so it refuses.\n\n## The maintainer decides\n\n- This PR does not carry a flipped Z into the program. It closes the issue by the second \"Done means\" clause.\n- A carry needs one new statement from the user: how the tool lengths of the flipped setup are measured. The decision file lists what that work includes.\n- If the maintainer wants the carry, the issue stays open or a new issue has that work. This PR files no new issue.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `a_flipped_z_refuses_by_name` (`crates/post/tests/wcs_flip.rs`, extended).\n- `a_flipped_z_without_a_cycle_names_the_tool_length_word_only` (`crates/post/tests/wcs_flip.rs`, new).\n- `a_flipped_z_refuses_the_post_by_name` (`crates/app/tests/wcs_flip_post.rs`, extended).\n\nRed before the fix:\n\n- The two post pins failed on unchanged code. The failure showed the old text.\n- The app pin failed with the old `setup_wcs_flip.rs`. The failure showed the old text.\n\nMutations:\n\n- Old `crates/post/src/post/wcs_flip.rs`: the two post pins are red. Restored: green.\n- Old `crates/app/src/setup_wcs_flip.rs`: the app pin is red. Restored: green.\n- The cycle clause printed for each section (`if true`): `a_flipped_z_without_a_cycle_names_the_tool_length_word_only` is red. Restored: green.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green: 8 steps, 0 failed (post lib, `wcs_flip`, `wcs_flip_dialects`, app lib, app `wcs_flip`, app `wcs_flip_post`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- The gate ran with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` and an empty `RUSTC_WRAPPER`. The sccache server of the build machine did not answer, and each build stopped after some crates.\n\nHeavy gate evidence from the latest review:\n\n- Command: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`.\n- Tested PR head: `21c04620607e3d66e5ee738c2dffc65445978c1e`.\n- Result: PASS, 184 steps, 0 failed, 21.6 minutes. The registered #1950 test failed at its expected assertion. The gate confirmed this expected failure.\n- The reviewer ran the heavy gate locally after a trial merge with main `744c0847b04d54cfc6e3e8b24a21520c40b6bcef`.\n- The final trial merge used main `f3b0e195503466db86b0ff0b15dbf614153e1bb4`. The app and dependency sources were unchanged between the two tested trees.\n- [All reached heavy lanes and their results](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2785#issuecomment-7018788718) appear in the latest review's detailed table. The table names each reached target and gives its pass count. A zero count means no ignored test ran in that target.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes. No posted program changes: the change is in refusal text only.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The `camcraft-ui` tests did not run. The UI code does not change. Its tests assert the words \"a flipped Z is not carried\", and the new text keeps them.\n- The statement about which dialects have G44 is from general machining knowledge. It was not checked against each control manual. The refusal text does not depend on it.\n- The machine door (`machine::untranslated_inversion`, an inverted machine Z) keeps its old text. It is not in the scope of this issue.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2714 touches the same file `crates/app/src/setup_wcs_flip.rs`, in a different function (`op_problem`). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: The refusal of a flipped WCS Z now names the exact reason: the post cannot know the tool-length word (G43 or G44) on a control that reads Z reversed.\n\nFixes #2474\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
